{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Wine and strong drink.</b> Rashi explains: the manner of intoxication. That is, the measure is enough for intoxication, as stated in tractate Keritot, chapter 'They said to him': Rabbi Eliezer says: 'wine and strong drink you shall not drink' — do not drink it in the manner of its intoxication; but if he interrupted with it, or if he put any amount of water into it, he is exempt." "<b>You shall not drink.</b> Even though they give wine and strong drink to other mourners, as it is written: 'give strong drink to him who is perishing, and wine to those of bitter soul' — <b>you and your sons shall not drink</b>, for it is not for you to practice the laws of mourning. And furthermore, you are forbidden in it, and there is in it a liability of death when you come into the Tent of Meeting, for it is not the way of a worshiper to be drunk."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:11:07.006533050Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}